The 157 branch's roll of V8 and Skia (bf32d15a65d04f5d23881d2dd4b48edf0a86d091,
refs/branch-heads/8103@{#1144}, after the 157.0.8103.45 tag): V8
0985c342965f..ed209c53fb33 (15.7.112.25 to 15.7.112.26) and Skia
ca220d775882..c2609d43d1ef, without their tests. Drop it once a 157 tag has it.

V8 e9dc5a2023f879c0966f25c126d18dd334d2932d (15.7@{#52}): "[maglev] Don't
reuse outer kReceiver call feedback in reduced apply" (crbugs 581669406 and
579313083, not public; no CVE listed yet; main commit
8e63f7dd778c9a440ebbedb276cbf57c8d21c3fa): when Function.prototype.apply
was reached through an outer call or apply reduction (such as
Function.prototype.apply.call(x)), Maglev took the outer call's kReceiver
feedback, which can even be a FeedbackCell, as the receiver of the inner
apply.

V8 ed209c53fb3395b4f4a0270db5e5a5bf9e2bbe70 (15.7@{#53}): Version 15.7.112.26.

Skia c2609d43d1efb837b13fe5e9f355083104e637ce (chrome/m157): "[Graphite]
Only allow clip path key bounds within int16_t" (crbugs 581669556 and
578656869, not public; no CVE listed yet; main commit
e6fe4f71440d7f5341acffedb8a8b03b514ef4c9): Graphite packed a clip path's
unclipped bounds into its cache key as 16-bit values without checking that
they fit, and OR'ed in their sign extension, so different clips could share
a key; bounds that don't fit are now keyed by the save record ID.

